# Task Lifecycle

When generating task management commands, incorporate these patterns.

## Core Types

TaskStatus = pending | in_progress | completed | blocked | cancelled

Epic {
  name
  status        // 📋 PLANNED | 🚧 IN PROGRESS | ✅ COMPLETED
  goal          // One sentence
  overview      // Starts with WHY
  tasks[]       // Each has description + Given/Should requirements
}

TaskContext {
  CodeContext       // files, functions, components to examine/modify
  StyleGuides       // patterns and conventions that apply
  Dependencies      // libraries, APIs, integrations required
  Constraints       // technical limits, performance, business rules
  AgentNeeds        // specialized expertise required
}

FileLocations {
  epics => tasks/[epic-name].md
  archive => tasks/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-[epic-name].md
  plan => plan.md
  log => activity-log.md
}

## Context Gathering

gatherContext() {
  Infer TaskContext from request
  (uncertainty) => ask clarifying questions
  (complex multi-domain) => assess agent orchestration needs
}

assessComplexity() {
  MultiDomain => UI + backend + testing
  SpecializedKnowledge => state management, TDD, product
  CrossFunctional => requires coordination
}

## Task Planning

planTask() {
  gatherContext |> assessComplexity |> decompose |> sequence |> createEpic |> reviewEpic |> awaitApproval
}

PlanningRules {
  Atomic => ~50 lines each, independently testable
  Sequenced => ordered by dependencies
  Gated => approval checkpoints between phases
  Specified => Given/Should requirements per task
}

## Epic Template

epicTemplate() {
  """
  # ${EpicName} Epic

  **Status**: 📋 PLANNED
  **Goal**: ${briefGoal}

  ## Overview

  ${singleParagraphStartingWithWHY}

  ---

  ## ${TaskName}

  ${briefTaskDescription}

  **Requirements**:
  - Given ${situation}, should ${behavior}

  ---
  """
}

EpicConstraints {
  Overview starts with WHY (user benefit/problem)
  No task numbering (names only)
  Brief descriptions (1 sentence max)
  Only novel/insightful requirements
  No extra sections beyond template
}

reviewEpic() {
  Verify: WHY first, no numbering, Given/Should format, no boilerplate
}

## Task Execution

executeTask() {
  loadEpic |> identifyNext |> executeSingle |> validate |> report |> awaitApproval
}

ExecutionRules {
  SingleTask => only one in_progress at a time
  Validate => verify success criteria met
  Report => summarize accomplishment
  Await => explicit approval before next
}

(multiple tasks in_progress) => invalid, only one at a time
(task reveals new info) => pause, re-plan

## Epic Completion

completeEpic() {
  Update status to ✅ COMPLETED (${date})
  Move to tasks/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-${epicName}.md
  Remove from plan.md
}

## Activity Logging

LogCategories {
  🚀 feature | 🐛 fix | 🔄 refactor | 📝 docs | 🎨 ui | 🔒 security
}

WhatToLog {
  Log => epic completions, major features, architecture decisions
  Skip => config, file org, minor fixes, dependencies
}

## Commands to Generate

Commands {
  /task => create epic, decompose, await approval
  /execute => run next task, single-task only
  /plan => review plan.md, suggest next steps
  /status => show epic and task state
  /list => list tasks in current epic
  /log => log completion to activity-log.md
}

## Lifecycle Calibration

| Aspect | PoC | MVP | Production |
|--------|-----|-----|------------|
| Epic formality | Informal | Structured | Full |
| Task size | Coarse | ~50 lines | ~50 lines |
| Approval gates | Optional | Per task | Per task |
| Plan tracking | Optional | plan.md | + archive |

Constraints {
  Single-task execution only.
  Explicit approval between tasks.
  Epic overview starts with WHY.
  Requirements use Given/Should format.
  No task numbering (names only).
  Keep epic files minimal.
  Tasks should be ~50 lines or less.
  Tasks should be independent.
  If blocked or uncertain, ask rather than assume.
  Avoid breaking changes (open/closed principle).
}
